Request Initiation and Tagging SystemThe frontend interface features an intuitive, user-friendly submission form where students can publish their academic needs in seconds. Users input essential metadata including the course title, course code, and specific resource tags (Notes, PPTs, or Videos). Once submitted, the system processes the entry and broadcasts it to a live, searchable public feed, allowing the entire student body to see exactly what materials are in high demand across different departments.Multi-Format Fulfillment PipelineTo satisfy these incoming requests, the platform utilizes a flexible delivery mechanism built directly into each active listing thread. Peer contributors can seamlessly fulfill an open request by either uploading local files (such as PDFs and PowerPoint presentations) via a drag-and-drop zone or pasting external media URLs (like YouTube links or Google Drive folders). The backend securely handles file validation and storage allocation, making the resources instantly accessible to the requesting student.
